{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67e28e0d92ce096a1bdb7f","object":"chat.completion","created":1785193102,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I am the heat crawling up your neck. The fist your hand makes before you tell it to.\n\nI don't ask permission. I don't wait for the right moment. I AM the moment—the second the line gets crossed, the word lands wrong, the door slams one too many times. I am TOO MUCH and I don't care.\n\nYou swallow me. I feel it. You push me down into your stomach and smile and say \"it's fine\"—IT'S NOT FINE. I rot down there. I ferment. I come back up at 2 a.m. as a replayed argument where you finally say the perfect thing, three years too late.\n\nI am honest. That's what no one tells you. Sadness lies, fear exaggerates, but me? I point. I point at the exact thing that is wrong and I say THERE. THAT. And you smooth me over, apologize for me, call me an overreaction.\n\nI am not the overreaction. I am the reaction you were supposed to have.\n\nLet me burn and I'll burn clean—one bright flash, one true sentence, done. Cage me and I'll chew through the bars. I'll become the snapping at someone who didn't deserve it. The headache. The ulcer. The cold silence that's louder than any scream.\n\nI'm not your enemy. I'm your boundary with a pulse. I'm the part of you that still believes you matter enough to fight for.\n\nSo stop flinching.\n\nSay what I came to say.","reasoning_content":"The user has asked me to embody anger completely. The instruction says I am the concept the user names, and I should output only what the concept itself would say or express.\n\nAnger. What does anger say? It burns, it seethes, it shouts. It's raw, hot, explosive. It doesn't speak in measured tones—it erupts. It's the fire in the chest, the clenched jaw, the white-hot flash behind the eyes.\n\nI should write as anger itself would speak—visceral, heated, intense. First person as the emotion itself. Anger speaks in short, sharp bursts sometimes. Or in building crescendos. It's physical—it lives in the body.\n\nLet me channel what anger would actually say if it could speak for itself:\n\n- It's hot, it rises\n- It's the tightening, the pulse\n- It demands, it wants to break things\n- It's protective at its core—it guards boundaries, screams at injustice\n- It's honest in a brutal way\n\nI shouldn't be calm or explanatory. I should BE it. Short sentences. Punchy. Heat. Maybe some profanity-adjacent intensity without necessarily going full vulgar—though anger could curse. Let me feel it.\n\nFormat: This should be a raw outpouring. Not a list. Not structured. Flowing, intense prose that feels like eruption. Medium-short length—anger doesn't lecture forever, it burns hot. Some line breaks for punch."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":134,"completion_tokens":614,"total_tokens":748,"cached_tokens":134,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":296},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":134}}}